{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"title":"Add Persistence","role":"article"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" turns persistence into a declare-and-register concern. You annotate a domain entity with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":"; the macro generates its SwiftData "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" “shadow” class, the value↔model converters, and the ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistableEntity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance. A generic ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntityDB","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" actor and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceCoordinator"},{"text":" build the container, synthesize one ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" per registered ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", and reuse the core ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for debounced, batched writes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reducers mutate plain value-type entities inside an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"; the plugin observes the changelog and writes through to SwiftData after a debounce. Reads happen once, at launch, into memory — the in-memory "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the source of truth."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For low-level manual wiring (writing your own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". For the macro details, see "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". To add cross-device iCloud sync on top, see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"anchor":"Before-you-start","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Before you start"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This guide assumes a Swidux app already exists — ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AppStore"},{"type":"text","text":" are wired and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If not, follow "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","isActive":true},{"text":" first.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"text":" is a local-only persistence layer. It needs ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"no iCloud, CloudKit, or Push entitlements","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — only the sandbox ","type":"text"},{"code":"com.apple.security.network.client","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement if your app also makes network calls (killswitch, analytics, feature flags). Adding sync entitlements to a local-only app is dead configuration and an App Review risk."}]},{"text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your app target in "},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPersistence\",","    ]",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Step 2: Annotate your domain entity with `@Persisted`","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Step-2-Annotate-your-domain-entity-with-Persisted"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A persisted entity is a value type that already satisfies "},{"code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ID == UUID"},{"type":"text","text":" (the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" contract). Add ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","    var createdAt: Date","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This generates a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CardModel: @Model"},{"type":"text","text":" class with "},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"toDomain()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"update(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", plus "},{"code":"extension Card: PersistableEntity { typealias Model = CardModel }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". By default every stored property is mirrored directly onto the model — SwiftData persists scalars "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"and","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" composites natively, so no manual blob columns are needed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"entity","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"state containers","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" slices). They are different layers and never apply to the same type.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Marker macros for non-trivial properties","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Marker-macros-for-non-trivial-properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A macro can’t infer relationships, foreign keys, or which fields are derived. Four property markers (named to avoid SwiftData’s own ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relationship"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"@Transient","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") tell ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" what to do:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","","    @Inline var styling: TextStyling                 \/\/ one opaque JSON Data column","    @ForeignKey var deckID: UUID                      \/\/ scalar parent reference","    @Relation(deleteRule: .cascade, inverse: \\TagModel.card)","    var tags: [Tag]                                   \/\/ SwiftData relationship","    @Ignored var renderedPreview: String?             \/\/ derived; omitted from the model","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Marker"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effect"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"(none)","type":"text"}]}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Mirror the property directly (SwiftData persists scalars and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" composites).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Force a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"text":" value into a single JSON ","type":"text"},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" column (keeps a CloudKit record compact; sidesteps SwiftData ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"-attribute edge cases).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@ForeignKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Intent marker on a ","type":"text"},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; functionally a mirrored scalar column.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Relation(deleteRule:inverse:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A SwiftData relationship to another ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" entity. The property’s type references the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"domain","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" type (","type":"text"},{"code":"[Tag]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tag?","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tag","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"); the model substitutes the ","type":"text"},{"code":"…Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" shadow. ","type":"text"},{"code":"inverse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a key path on the generated model, e.g. ","type":"text"},{"code":"\\TagModel.card","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"code":"deleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxDeleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":".cascade","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".nullify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".noAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".deny","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"@Ignored","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Exclude a derived\/denormalized property. Must be optional so it can be reconstructed as ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on load.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"style":"note","name":"Note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not generate an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Attribute(.unique)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — CloudKit forbids unique constraints. Identity is enforced by upsert-by-","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" inside ","type":"text"},{"code":"EntityDB","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the same generated model works for both local and synced containers.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"anchor":"Step-3-Put-the-EntityStore-on-your-state","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 3: Put the `EntityStore` on your state"},{"code":["@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    var cards: EntityStore<Card> = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Your reducers mutate ","type":"text"},{"code":"state.cards","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" like any ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"state.cards[card.id] = card","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"state.cards.modify(id) { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"state.cards[id] = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Every change is recorded for the plugin to drain.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Step-4-Build-the-coordinator-and-register-the-plugin","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 4: Build the coordinator and register the plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", build a local container, create a ","type":"text"},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", register its plugin, and run first-load hydration before constructing the store:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","extension Store where State == AppState, Action == AppAction {","    static func configured() async -> AppStore {","        let container = try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","","        let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","            entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","            container: container,","            debounce: .milliseconds(250)","        )","","        let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","        \/\/ Register UndoPlugin first if you use it — snapshots must precede writes.","        plugins.register(persistence.corePlugin)","","        var initial = AppState()","        await persistence.hydrate(into: &initial)   \/\/ first-load: fill EntityStores from disk","","        return Store(initialState: initial, reducer: { … }, plugins: plugins)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"hydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"first-load only","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — it replaces each ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" with the on-disk rows before any live edits exist. The only refresh path after launch is ","type":"text"},{"code":"rehydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which always ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"merges","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (preferring in-memory values) so a “refresh from disk” can never clobber unflushed writes or in-progress UI edits.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Step-5-Flush-on-background","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 5: Flush on background"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Writes are debounced, so drain them when the app is backgrounded or terminates:","type":"text"}]},{"code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .background {","        Task { await persistence.corePlugin.flush() }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"anchor":"Multiple-entities-and-ordering","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Multiple entities and ordering"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Register one ","type":"text"},{"code":".entity(\\.keyPath)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" per ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.decks), .entity(\\.cards), .entity(\\.tags)],","    container: try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(","        models: [DeckModel.self, CardModel.self, TagModel.self]","    )",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pass every generated ","type":"text"},{"code":"…Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" type to the container’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"models:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Writers flush in registration order — if entity B holds a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Relation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to A, register A’s entity first.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Testing","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Testing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The whole stack runs against an in-memory SwiftData store, so persistence is unit-testable with no disk and no CloudKit:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let container = try ContainerFactory.makeInMemoryContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","let db = EntityDB(modelContainer: container)","","try await db.upsert(Card(id: id, quote: \"hi\", createdAt: .now), as: CardModel.self)","let all = try await db.fetchAll(CardModel.self)","#expect(all.first?.quote == \"hi\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To prove the rule-#8 merge guarantee, seed the store, make a live in-memory edit, call ","type":"text"},{"code":"coordinator.rehydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and assert the live edit survives.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plugin and the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"How-to-Guides","t